From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:38:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 153/153] PC5: a 32-bit game gets the room above 2 GiB, the space it
 can have, and the Windows error when memory runs out (Wine patches 1018 to
 1021)

A 32-bit program had a 4 GiB limit (0921), but only the low 2 GiB was reserved, so the console's own mappings could take the rest and the space the game saw as free above 2 GiB wasn't all there: a game that reserves the largest free block it finds for its heap asked for 2 GiB, got nothing and read through a null pointer (Wanted: Weapons of Fate). The range above 2 GiB is now reserved for a program with 4 GiB (1018), VirtualQuery reports only reserved space as free below 4 GiB (1020), and the first two allocations that find no room log what fills the space (1019). A commit the console has no memory for now fails with Windows' commitment-limit error and leaves the pages as they were, instead of an access-denied error a game takes for a bug (V8's "Check failed: 1455L == error."), and the direct-memory layer logs the calls the kernel refuses with the pool's largest free block (1021). From leolobato/prospero-win's 1000, 1005, 1007 and 1020.
